(text "ASSEMBLY, BRING-UP AND MOUNTING NOTES" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 17.000 0) (effects (font (size 3.0 3.0) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e2ae5635-3ba6-426c-b168-69d66e33eb3a"))
(text "Boards ordered as JLCPCB turnkey (SMT + THT terminals); Teensy and its headers are hand-fitted." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 21.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d60685c8-098d-456f-9ff0-2bb3f4688a4f"))
(polyline (pts (xy 14.000 23.000) (xy 418.000 23.000)) (stroke (width 0.3) (type solid)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "df050e1f-16c2-4673-8dd3-b936352e034f"))
(text "1. TEENSY 4.1 (U1) - HAND SOLDER" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 28.000 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "fafed8d9-3c9c-4805-a40d-097586b3fb0b"))
(text "Solder two 1x24 female headers (HC-PM254-8.5H-1x24PZ, C41376163) into the U1 footprint, then plug the Teensy in." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 32.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "30aa5fa5-ad6c-447e-8d05-1dab60104f33"))
(text "CUT the VIN-VUSB pad on the underside of the Teensy (near the USB connector) with a knife: the board feeds Teensy VIN from the 5 V buck through D9." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 36.700 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "37cc5283-db63-4193-aa0d-08d2b802bbad"))
(text "Do not connect USB and an external 5 V to VIN without this cut. USB programming then works with the board powered or unpowered (D9 isolates)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 40.900 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "35273cc6-87c3-499b-81f1-40de6f744554"))
(text "No battery is fitted (VBAT unconnected). Programming button/ON-OFF pads are not wired." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 45.100 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3da53107-5b21-48c2-84e5-0255fb6d8859"))
(text "2. HX711 RATE JUMPERS (SJ1-SJ3)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 52.300 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e11c692d-4780-485c-b165-3d16f551e95d"))
(text "Each HX711 RATE pin goes to the centre pad of a 3-way solder jumper: default bridge 1-2 = +3V3 = 80 SPS." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 56.800 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c6993441-4540-4310-abde-2d73f346e3be"))
(text "To run 10 SPS: cut the 1-2 bridge with a knife and bridge 2-3 (GND). RATE high is referenced to DVDD = 3.3 V." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 61.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1cd0dd97-a5db-4209-9881-b5fe43819b7c"))
(text "Firmware: read all three HX711 DOUT lines together on the shared SCK (pins 3, 0, 1 and clock pin 2)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 65.200 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ae1958eb-c12d-4e09-b5d6-89b9d7bad33a"))
(text "3. E-STOP WIRING (J32) AND FIRST POWER-UP" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 72.400 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d7ec2f9e-8141-4e78-ae46-c058b3b63777"))
(text "Wire the E-stop NC contact block(s) to J32: contact A pins 1-2, contact B pins 3-4 (see sheet 4). Fit E-stop (or a jumper across pins 1-2) BEFORE applying 12 V or the valves will stay off." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 76.900 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "490e0bbd-16e2-42eb-b33d-93ee58777513"))
(text "Power up with no valves attached: measure +5 V (C1) and +3V3, check Teensy powers and ESTOP_IN reads HIGH with E-stop closed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 81.100 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "800e837d-efac-4216-8307-8fa72fec258d"))
(text "Press E-stop: +12V_VALVE must drop to 0 V while +5 V / +3V3 / Teensy stay on; ESTOP_IN reads LOW. Release (reset) and valves re-arm automatically: add a firmware latch." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 85.300 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "35e3c099-fb0a-452d-bf6c-bcde8c380d75"))
(text "With a bench supply set to 12 V / 1 A first, then 15 A supply with valves on." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 89.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4ef850dd-7ff1-4da5-88c6-3fe2498f3061"))
(text "4. 12 V INPUT" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 96.700 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "22aaf303-77ac-4423-85c3-67556a348d58"))
(text "Use >= 14 AWG for the supply lead. F1 is a Littelfuse 178.6165 ATO/ATC holder at the front edge (below J16)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 101.200 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ea494883-0ca4-4ad5-9a25-fbf4e8495e82"))
(text "The 20 A ATO blade fuse is user supplied and is not in the BOM or the JLCPCB shipment." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 105.400 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f8b8090e-d178-4b47-8da4-bcfc2cd8149d"))
(text "If the fuse blows, find the fault, then pull the fuse straight out from the front edge (board on standoffs)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 109.600 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "77ba1485-bf89-42ea-974a-c4ae8de416ab"))
(text "and fit a new 20 A ATO/ATC automotive blade fuse (standard regular size, typically yellow)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 113.800 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "326c3e6e-0222-4c9a-b36a-f8a0670712ba"))
(text "A reversed supply is blocked by Q8 (nothing downstream is powered; the fuse does not blow)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 118.000 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "65738366-7ac2-41b8-89f1-3efc504097d4"))
(text "Supply must be 12 V DC +/- 10% at >= 15 A (all 7 valves ON) or sequence the valves in firmware." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 122.200 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4fefc521-69bb-44dc-b5f3-a775bbdc8bab"))
(text "Holder body ~8 mm tall; an inserted ATO fuse stands ~20 mm above the board." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 126.400 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6afad94c-e072-4412-86cd-673a5fb8f405"))
(text "If components face the L-bracket, use ~25 mm standoffs or let the holder sit past the bracket edge." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 130.600 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b91fe284-52c1-4b02-9ddd-91d9089a3686"))
(text "If components face away from the bracket, no extra standoff height is needed." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 134.800 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ecc7eb46-8209-40f9-847f-dddff9d2b43f"))
(text "5. MOUNTING (L-BRACKET)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 14.000 142.000 0) (effects (font (size 2.4 2.4) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6b5254f3-8bc5-4edf-8117-3e5b71df0d98"))
(text "Four M3 holes (3.2 mm NPTH) 4.0 mm from each board edge: hole centres 134.5 mm x 130.0 mm apart (sheet 8)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 146.500 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0a7cb823-2db9-4582-96ee-2185b047626d"))
(text "Use M3 standoffs (nylon or metal) 8-10 mm tall under the bracket: the board must not touch the bracket (copper keepout 7 mm diameter around each hole)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 150.700 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4affb17c-1167-4c89-903c-d565f22739b8"))
(text "Panel wiring (E-stop, switches on DI_1..DI_8, displays J29-J31) enters from the front edge where terminals face out." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.000 154.900 0) (effects (font (size 1.9 1.9)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "547935cf-2485-42b5-a38c-3cced46cf7aa"))
